Q: How to minimize number of lookups in a Hash? A: <blockquote>
<p>Back to the <code>default_proc</code> - as I understand it, it does <em>not</em> return the default value. It has to <em>assign</em> it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Whether you assign it or not is up to you. If you don't assign it, the key will remain unset. For example, this will keep returning the current time for unknown keys, leaving the hash empty:</p>
<pre class="lang-rb prettyprint-override"><code>h = {}
h.default_proc = -&gt;(h, k) { Time.now }

h[:foo] #=&gt; 2026-04-15 15:30:51.312987 +0200 # &lt;- return value from default_proc
h[:foo] #=&gt; 2026-04-15 15:31:09.962173 +0200 # &lt;- return value from default_proc

h #=&gt; {}
</code></pre>
<p>Whereas this will <em>assign</em> the current time for an unknown key in addition to returning it, thus populating the hash as a side-effect:</p>
<pre class="lang-rb prettyprint-override"><code>h = {}
h.default_proc = -&gt;(h, k) { h[k] = Time.now }

h[:foo] #=&gt; 2026-04-15 15:33:39.566583 +0200 # &lt;- return value from default_proc
h[:foo] #=&gt; 2026-04-15 15:33:39.566583 +0200 # &lt;- stored value for :foo

h #=&gt; {foo: 2026-04-15 15:33:39.566583 +0200}
</code></pre>

Q: Read and write binary data to postgresql from dart server app A: <p><code>result[0]</code> is the whole row, not the <code>bytea</code> value.</p>
<p>Use the column inside the row:</p>
<pre><code>final result = await dB.execute(
  'SELECT data FROM accounts WHERE username = \$1',
  parameters: ['janedoe'],
);

final bytes = result.first[0] as List&lt;int&gt;;
final account = Account.fromBuffer(bytes);
</code></pre>
